              '<div class="head"><span class="drug mono">codeine</span><span class="verdict">Not called from an uploaded VCF</span></div>\n'
              '<p class="prose">This gene’s result depends on structural and copy-number changes that need specialised analysis of the sequencing reads, which this application does not perform. No VCF uploaded here will resolve it — it needs a specialised test or caller. The system declines to guess rather than report a genotype it cannot support.</p>\n'
              '<p class="note">Nothing about the uploaded file would change this result.</p>\n'
              '</article>\n'
              '\n'
              '<h2>Input coverage</h2>\n'
              '<p class="note">How many of the positions each gene needs carried a usable genotype in the uploaded file. A genotype caller reads an absent position as matching the reference, so missing data can produce confident results rather than uncertain ones — which is why the count is printed whether or not it passed, and why a gene below its minimum is reported as Unknown.</p>\n'
